# Code Style & Quality

## Standard & flags

- **C11** (`-std=c11`)
- `-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror`
- `-D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200809L`
- Zero warnings — all treated as errors

## Formatting

- **Indentation:** 4 spaces. No tabs.
- **Function definitions:** opening brace on its own line.
- **Line length:** prefer ≤80 characters where practical.
- **Files end with a single newline.**

## Module conventions

- **`src/main.c`** stays thin — wiring only; dispatch help, version, or
  extra-args notice, then `return EXIT_SUCCESS`. No business logic beyond flag
  dispatch.
- **One concern per `src/true_toto_*.c`** — do not collapse back into a
  monolith without reason.
- **Platform code:** use `#if defined(_WIN32)` / `#else` for OS-specific
  behaviour where needed.

## Naming

| Kind | Style | Examples |
|------|-------|----------|
| Functions | `snake_case` | `scan_meta_flags`, `print_help`, `print_version` |
| Enums / enum values | `snake_case` / `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` | `true_toto_flag`, `TRUE_TOTO_HELP` |
| Macros / constants | `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` | `TRUE_TOTO_VERSION_STRING`, `TRUE_TOTO_EXIT_OK` |
| Headers | `TRUE_TOTO_*_H` guards | `TRUE_TOTO_H`, `TRUE_TOTO_CLI_H` |

Public API prefix: **`true_toto_`** for module entry points. Internal CLI
helpers (`scan_meta_flags`, `print_help`, `print_version`,
`print_extra_args_notice`) are declared in `true_toto_cli.h` and implemented in
`true_toto_cli.c`.

## Memory

- No dynamic allocation required. Stack only throughout.
- No `malloc`, `calloc`, `realloc`, or `free` anywhere in this project.

## Output rules

- **No output when `argc == 1`.** Extra non-meta args trigger the fixed stdout
  notice via `print_extra_args_notice()`. `main()` returns `EXIT_SUCCESS`.
- `--help`, `--version`, and extra-args notice text is written via
  `write(STDOUT_FILENO, …)` for consistency with the coreutils-style family.
  Do not use `printf` / `fprintf` / `fputs` for this output.
- On write failure: call `true_toto_emit_error`, then exit `1`.

## Errors

- **stderr only:** `true-toto: <context>: <strerror(errno)>`
- Implemented in `true_toto_emit.c`

## Comments

- Chain-of-thought block at top of each `src/*.c` and test file (see existing
  files). Include: responsibility, syscalls used, heap usage, C standard.
- Contract comments on non-trivial functions: preconditions, postconditions,
  return value, error behaviour.
- Comment non-obvious decisions (exit code rationale, platform guards); not
  obvious code.

## Tests

- Plain `assert()` — no external test framework.
- One scenario per `tests/test_scan_*.c`; runner in `tests/test_runner.c`.
- Print `PASS: <name>` on success.

## What not to do

- Do not compile as C++.
- Do not link libraries beyond libc.
- Do not use `gets`, unbounded `scanf`.
- Do not add stdout output beyond the documented help, version, and
  extra-args notice paths.
- Do not add `-h` / `-v` (single-dash) — only `--help`, `--h`, `--version`,
  and `--v` are special.
- Do not add signal handlers — `true-toto` exits immediately and has no loop
  to interrupt.

